# Frontend conventions

- Named exports only: `export function Foo()`. No `export default`.
- Import from the `src` root (`components/…`, `pages/…`, `services/…`,
  `data/…`). Relative paths only inside a component folder.
- `import type` is required for type-only imports (`verbatimModuleSyntax`).
- UI strings are French; identifiers, files and comments are English.

## Chakra only, with strict tokens

The theme sets `strictTokens: true`. Token-backed props must use design tokens.

```tsx
// BAD
<Box padding="12px" color="#fff" gap="0.5rem" />
// GOOD
<Box padding="3" color="fg" gap="2" />
```

Use the compound-component API and wrap floating content in `Portal`:
`Select.Root` / `Popover.Root` with `.Trigger`, `.Positioner`, `.Content`.
Icons come from `react-icons/lu` (`react-icons/md` where no `lu` equivalent
exists). Do not add Tailwind, CSS modules or another styling layer.

One exception: `components/StoryDisplayer/storyDisplayer.css` styles the raw SVG
diagram, which cannot use Chakra props. Reach the theme from there with
`var(--chakra-colors-fg)` and friends rather than hardcoding neutrals.

## Typed config objects

Derive unions from data with `as const satisfies`, never with `enum`
(`erasableSyntaxOnly` forbids enums).

## The chapter diagram is hand-drawn

`components/StoryDisplayer/` owns an SVG of several hundred chapters, so it
breaks the usual "everything through state" habit on purpose:

- `usePanZoom` writes the `viewBox` attribute directly on the element, and the
  search highlight toggles a class on the chapter's `<g>`. Do not move either
  into React state.
- Anything that has to follow the view (the minimap) subscribes with
  `panZoom.subscribe`, which fires outside React.
- The rendered scene sits behind a `useMemo` keyed on the layout. Keep new
  per-chapter rendering inside it.

## Gotchas

- Tabs use `lazyMount` + `unmountOnExit`; page components remount on every tab
  switch, so do not keep state that must survive there. Book layouts survive it
  through the cache in `services/graphLayout.ts`.
- `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` is off. Use `array.at(i)` when an element may be
  missing; a guard on `array[i]` is reported as an unnecessary condition.
- Assets must not use absolute URLs; the Pages base path is
  `/grimoire-de-dagda/`.
